{UTF-8}
{ Chapter 12: out of control (fixes that fail). When output falls short of demand, maintenance hours are moved to production; the maintenance backlog grows and machines break down more. }
Base Demand=
	360
	~	unit/week
	~	|
Demand Increase=
	36
	~	unit/week
	~	Extra demand from week 10 (10%).
	|
Demand=
	Base Demand + STEP(Demand Increase, 10)
	~	unit/week
	~	|
Hours Available=
	500
	~	hour/week
	~	Machine hours the plant has each week.
	|
Normal Maintenance Hours=
	50
	~	hour/week
	~	Hours planned for preventive maintenance.
	|
Fix Sensitivity=
	5
	~	dmnl
	~	Share of maintenance hours moved to production per unit of perceived shortfall fraction (0: no fix).
	|
Maintenance Hours=
	Normal Maintenance Hours * MAX(0, 1 - Fix Sensitivity * Perceived Shortfall)
	~	hour/week
	~	The fix: fewer maintenance hours when output falls short.
	|
Normal Breakdowns=
	0.2
	~	dmnl
	~	Share of scheduled production hours lost to breakdowns at the normal maintenance backlog.
	|
Normal Backlog=
	72
	~	hour
	~	Maintenance backlog when maintenance keeps pace with wear.
	|
Breakdown Fraction=
	MIN(0.9, Normal Breakdowns * Maintenance Backlog / Normal Backlog)
	~	dmnl
	~	|
Production Hours=
	(Hours Available - Maintenance Hours) * (1 - Breakdown Fraction)
	~	hour/week
	~	|
Units per Hour=
	1
	~	unit/hour
	~	|
Output=
	Production Hours * Units per Hour
	~	unit/week
	~	|
Shortfall=
	MAX(0, Demand - Output) / Demand
	~	dmnl
	~	Fraction of demand not met.
	|
Perception Time=
	2
	~	week
	~	Time for management to see the shortfall.
	|
Perceived Shortfall=
	SMOOTHI(Shortfall, Perception Time, 0)
	~	dmnl
	~	|
Wear per Production Hour=
	0.1
	~	hour/hour
	~	Maintenance work created by each production hour.
	|
Wear Added=
	Production Hours * Wear per Production Hour
	~	hour/week
	~	|
Minimum Maintenance Time=
	2
	~	week
	~	Fastest time to clear the maintenance backlog with enough hours.
	|
Maintenance Done=
	MIN(Maintenance Hours, Maintenance Backlog / Minimum Maintenance Time)
	~	hour/week
	~	|
Maintenance Backlog= INTEG(
	Wear Added - Maintenance Done,
	72)
	~	hour
	~	Maintenance work needed and not yet done.
	|
INITIAL TIME = 0 ~ week ~ |
FINAL TIME = 104 ~ week ~ |
TIME STEP = 0.0625 ~ week ~ |
SAVEPER = 0.0625 ~ week ~ |
